sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as 👤 Public Anonymous User
    participant Frontend as 🖥️ Next.js Web App
    participant Middleware as 🛡️ Express API Middleware
    participant Controller as 🎮 Express Controller / Services
    participant ProtectedResource as 🎯 Verification Pipeline

    Note over User,ProtectedResource: v1 Hackathon Architecture: Anonymous Public Access (No User Accounts / Login)

    User->>Frontend: Accesses web interface & submits video URL
    Frontend->>Middleware: POST /api/videos/process (Public request, no Bearer token)

    Note over Middleware: Security Enforcement without Authentication
    Middleware->>Middleware: 1. CORS Origin Validation
    Middleware->>Middleware: 2. Rate Limiting Middleware (IP-based protection against quota abuse)
    Middleware->>Middleware: 3. Input Validation (Zod schema checking for YouTube URL format)

    alt Security / Rate Limit Check Fails
        Middleware-->>Frontend: 429 Too Many Requests / 400 Bad Request
        Frontend-->>User: Displays error message
    else Security Checks Pass
        Middleware->>Controller: Forwards validated request
        Controller->>ProtectedResource: Executes verification pipeline
        ProtectedResource-->>Controller: Returns verdict data
        Controller-->>Frontend: 200 OK with claim ledger payload
        Frontend-->>User: Displays verified claims ledger
    end

    Note over User,ProtectedResource: -------------------------------------------------------------
    Note over User,ProtectedResource: Future Authentication Extension Point [STATUS: TBD / DEFERRED]
    Note over User,ProtectedResource: In v2 (Post-Hackathon), an Auth Middleware (e.g. Supabase Auth / JWT)
    Note over User,ProtectedResource: will attach at step 2 to verify sessions for saved history & user accounts.
